    <fr-refs>FR-02</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add ONE additive entry to the EXISTING regarding write map so the association engine can write a report-card association. This extends `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs` — it does NOT add a new map, a new regarding mechanism, or a new engine (ADR-024 / ADR-045: one regarding mechanism; extend, never fork).

    Add the mapping `sprk_reportcard` (the report-card record type) → `sprk_regardingreportcard` (the regarding lookup on `sprk_communication`), mirroring the exact shape/convention of the 6 existing entries in `RegardingFieldMap` (matter, project, invoice, work assignment, budget, service request). Use the EXACT logical names task 001 confirmed live: the `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup logical name from the 001 note, and the report-card record-type code / `sprk_recordtype_ref` row (RPTC) it maps from. Do NOT hardcode any numbering scheme — the entry maps the record type to its regarding lookup only; the number-field roster lives in `sprk_recordtype_ref` (read by the identifier rung, task 020).

    Consume task 001's verification note for the exact `sprk_regardingreportcard` logical name + the RPTC row shape. Add/extend the characterization test that proves the engine writes the correct regarding lookup for a report-card match. This is the SINGLE map entry — the identifier rung that MATCHES a report-card number is task 020; the auto-file policy is 021.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication Association Engine. Authority on `Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs` and the ADR-024 polymorphic regarding family (write only via the resolver; one regarding mechanism). Fluent in ADR-045 (extend the engine, never fork), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification, and the additive/non-breaking discipline for shared `Services/Communication/` code.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `RegardingFieldMap.cs` gains a single additive `sprk_reportcard`→`sprk_regardingreportcard` entry mirroring the 6 existing entries, using the exact logical names task 001 confirmed live. The engine can write a report-card association through the existing resolver path — no second map, no second regarding mechanism, no numbering scheme in code. Build clean; a characterization test proves the engine resolves a report-card match to the `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup; existing regarding-map tests stay green; publish-size delta ≈0 + no new HIGH CVE reported; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The Association Engine writes a matched record's association via a typed regarding lookup on `sprk_communication`, selected by `RegardingFieldMap` keyed on record type. It ships with the 6 non-report-card core types; the report card was added as an operator prerequisite (the `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup + the `sprk_recordtype_ref` RPTC row, verified in 001) but the code map has no entry, so the engine cannot write a report-card association (FR-02). This task adds that one entry.

      §11 Component Justification: (1) **Existing** — `RegardingFieldMap` already owns the record-type→regarding-lookup map for the other 6 core types (grep-confirmed); there is no report-card entry. (2) **Extension** — this is ONE additive dictionary entry reusing the existing map + resolver path; it introduces no new service, map, or mechanism. (3) **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete)** — without the entry the engine cannot write a report-card association even when the identifier rung (020) matches a report-card number; FR-02 fails and success-criterion 1 (report-card association) cannot pass. Named contract failure, not "future flexibility."

      Numbering schemes stay OUT of code (spec MUST rule; CLAUDE.md): this entry maps the record type to its regarding lookup only. The report-card NUMBER match (reverse-lookup against `sprk_reportcardnumber`) is the identifier rung's job (020), driven by `sprk_recordtype_ref`.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs (ADD the `sprk_reportcard`→`sprk_regardingreportcard` entry, mirroring the 6 existing entries)</file>
