      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs (downstream — status mapping consumes a resolved regarding write)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-02">Scope: add ONLY the `sprk_reportcard`→`sprk_regardingreportcard` entry to `RegardingFieldMap.cs`, mirroring the 6 existing entries; the engine can then write a report-card association. Nothing else.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Scope: write the regarding via the existing resolver/map — ONE regarding mechanism. MUST NOT add a second map, a second regarding mechanism, or a bespoke report-card write path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Scope: extend the existing engine map additively; MUST NOT fork the engine or add a second engine. Existing entries + tests stay untouched/green (non-breaking).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (numbering out of code)">Scope: the entry maps record type → regarding lookup only. MUST NOT hardcode any report-card numbering scheme in code; the number-field roster lives in `sprk_recordtype_ref` (read by 020).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification in the PR (extends the existing `RegardingFieldMap` — no new mechanism); report publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0, no new packages); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`; `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §11">Scope: Component Justification — one additive entry; state the concrete FR-02 failure mode prevented (engine cannot write a report-card association) with grep evidence that no report-card entry exists.</constraint>
  </constraints>

